WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.660
In 1964, a Londoner who had been ordained
as a Buddhist monk in India came home

2
00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:06.900
to England.

3
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:12.940
In 1967 he founded a new movement:
a Buddhism for the modern West.

4
00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.170
In many traditions, the
sangha has two parts:

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.700
monks and nuns, and the lay
people who support them.

6
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.640
So can you be fully ordained as a
Buddhist while keeping your job,

7
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.690
your home and your partner?

8
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.290
In this mission, you'll meet the
movement now called Triratna,

9
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.620
and its founder, Sangharakshita.

10
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.660
Then you'll see what it
means by going for refuge,

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.970
and who can join its Order.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: find out whether
ordination can fit a job,

13
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.110
a home and a partner.
